  "claim_short": "If a real homogeneous polynomial F of even degree satisfies F(x)>0 for every nonzero x and its Hessian is invertible for every nonzero x, then the Hessian is in fact positive definite at every nonzero point and F is strictly convex. The tensor nonnegativity and irreducibility assumptions from the surrounding source theorem are not needed.",
